  "type": "multipleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "If the adjoint of a $3 \\times 3$ matrix $P$ is $\\left[\\begin{array}{lll}1 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3\\end{array}\\right]$, then the possible value(s) of the determinant of $P$ is (are)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ZZEkD",
      "text": "$-2$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "NvtJg",
      "text": "$-1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "qVdLq",
      "text": "1",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zQNGP",
      "text": "2",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know for a third order matrix $P$,\r\n\r\n$|\\operatorname{Adj} P|=|P|^{2}$\r\n\r\nWhere\r\n\r\n$\\begin{aligned}\r\n\r\n&|\\operatorname{Adj} P|=1(3-7)-4(6-7)+4(2-1)=4 \\\\\r\n\r\n\\therefore \\quad &|P|^{2}=4 \\mathrm{P}|P|=2 \\text { or }-2\r\n\r\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
